The source below is intended to export `createObservableRecord(initial)`. `initial` must be a non-null, non-array object or cause `TypeError`. The returned object exposes `get(key)`, `set(key, value)`, and `subscribe(listener)`. `get` returns the current value. `set` stores the value and synchronously calls current listeners in subscription order with `(key, value, previousValue)`; it must notify even when values are equal. `subscribe` requires a function, adds it once per subscription call, and returns an idempotent unsubscribe function that removes only that subscription. Listener additions or removals during a notification affect only later `set` calls. Initial data must be shallow-copied, and the input must not be mutated. Correct the single bug and return the complete source file.

```javascript
'use strict';

function createObservableRecord(initial) {
  if (initial === null || typeof initial !== 'object' || Array.isArray(initial)) {
    throw new TypeError('initial must be an object');
  }

  const data = { ...initial };
  const listeners = [];

  function get(key) {
    return data[key];
  }

  function set(key, value) {
    const previousValue = data[key];
    data[key] = value;
    for (const entry of listeners) {
      if (entry.active) {
        entry.listener(key, value, previousValue);
      }
    }
  }

  function subscribe(listener) {
    if (typeof listener !== 'function') {
      throw new TypeError('listener must be a function');
    }
    const entry = { listener, active: true };
    listeners.push(entry);
    return function unsubscribe() {
      entry.active = false;
    };
  }

  return { get, set, subscribe };
}

module.exports = { createObservableRecord };
```

